{number: 146}
{title: O the Help that God has Given}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O, the help that God has given,
Through His grace unto this hour,
O, His love which never faileth,
Wondrous grace and wondrous pow’r,
Day and night, he never guides us,
Keeps us in His loving care.
Yes, in Him all things are possible
For the glory of our God.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
I am weak of frame and spirit,
But the Lord has strengthened me,
He has poured His grace upon me,
So that I can want no more.
Through the valley and the desert,
I am singing as I go,
For my Master walks beside me,
Holding my hand where e’er we go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
{end_of_verse}
